lf will pause in other problems i  did have to shield but my positions  harlow many people across the country  had it much worse off than me and they  suffered terribly by not being able to  see their  relatives uh or or people you know sadly  passing away and not being able to see  their loved ones as they were  dying so we all feel um hugely let down  by what has  gone on it shouldn't have happened i had  constituents talking to me about it only  yesterday in harlow how upset they were  as to what had happened in downing  street and what i've called for is for  three hours from the  uh prime minister for him to respond to  the  anguish of the public to take  responsibility for what has happened and  to reset the government and focus on the  genuine people's priorities like uh what  we've just been talking about robert  robert is there a four are possibly  there which is resign  i'm not agitating against the promise  i'm certainly not putting a no  confidence motion for two reasons first  of all i don't think the public would  welcome bloodletting or change of  government in the midst of a crisis in  terms of eastern europe in terms of uh  the economy and the cost of living  coming out of kobe and secondly i do  accept that i owe the prime minister  some residual loyalty not just for  winning the 2019 election and for brexit  but also for the vaccine program for the  jobs miracle we've got  in our country and uh i think those are  important things to  to to remember but that doesn't mean as  i say i don't want uh the pr i want the  prime minister to take responsibility to  reset the government and respond  properly to the public

